  "name": "bolero",
  "description": "Bolero is a unified testing facade for Rust that integrates coverage-guided fuzzing, property-based testing, and formal verification into a single developer workflow. It leverages a trait-based input generation system to transform raw byte streams from engines like AFL, LibFuzzer, and Honggfuzz into structured types, while also supporting symbolic execution through Kani. The framework includes a specialized CLI for managing test targets, corpus maintenance, and failure reduction across diverse execution environments.",
